From 39405d7dc6640fdde3b35f2cd81230973c6950ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lihao Ran <30372757+Lumosis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:38:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] [Bugfix][Core] MTP: keep GDN state across scheduling gaps
 (#1811)

* fix(mtp): preserve GDN checkpoints across scheduling gaps

Keep the last written unified checkpoint column and compact state slot
while a request still owns its KV state, including batches where it is
not scheduled. Release stale slot ownership on finish, preemption, and
resume before recomputation. This prevents wrong checkpoint reads and
cross-request recurrent-state reuse after a scheduling gap.

Reject resumable input sessions at the standard input frontend when a
compact Mamba pool cannot retain their state within its running-request
capacity. Ordinary requests and streaming output remain supported.

Validation: 125 focused CPU tests; 544 unified cases and 16 compact
configurations; 17 async contract tests on each of 8 TPU ranks; 40 GDN
kernel comparisons with exact output equality; 8192 alternating-request
raw-pool steps without invalid reads or nonfinite outputs.

Ruff and applicable non-type pre-commit checks pass. Pyrefly retains the
same 12 minimal-environment / 17 full-runtime baseline errors, with no
new diagnostics. An unrelated idle-DP test fixture failure reproduces
on the base source. Full model-service acceptance-rate load testing was
not performed.

Signed-off-by: yanzecheng.yzc <yanzecheng.yzc@alibaba-inc.com>
(cherry picked from commit f38957a984fb2bc8e47e13752a7f62d05c22d03b)
Signed-off-by: Lihao Ran <imlihao.ran@gmail.com>

* test(runner): give the read-offset migration fixture live requests

The seed-copy collector now keeps a request's last written checkpoint
column while the request is in `self.requests`, not only while it is in
the persistent batch. TestUnifiedReadOffsetMigration builds its runner
from MagicMock(spec=TPUModelRunner), which has no `requests` attribute,
so all four of its tests raised AttributeError after the previous
commit. Populate `requests` with the batch's request IDs, as the other
fixtures touched by that commit do.

Signed-off-by: Lihao Ran <imlihao.ran@gmail.com>

